    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1034">

                <pb facs="1202" n="1006" xml:id="pg1006"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/7–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1034<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador
                        in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d1034-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-29">July 29, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 406. To American Embassy London repeated
                    for information to State Department, Washington. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Victory</hi> 406. TopSec.</p>
                <p>Re London’s 65460, July 26th repeated to Department as 7546 <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Comea</hi> 343.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1034-f2"/></p>
                <p>The President has approved the EAC agreement of July 26th amending protocol of
                    September 12th 1944 on zones occupation Germany and administration greater
                    Berlin, together with covering report and accompanying exchanges of letters.
                    Please inform EAC colleagues that United States Government has approved EAC
                        agreement.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1034-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1034-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1034-f1-content">
                <p>Printed from the text received in the Department of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1034-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1034-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. This message informed Byrnes that the additional requirements
                    agreement (see <ref target="#d1038">document No. 1038</ref>) had been signed on
                    July 25, and that the agreement on zones of occupation in Germany would be
                    signed on July 26.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1034-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1034-f3-content">
                <p>Winant executed this instruction on July 29. Notification of approval was given
                    by the other signatories as follows: the United Kingdom on August 2, the
                    Provisional Government of the French Republic on August 7, and the Soviet Union
                    on August 13.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
